{"availability":"available","full":"lukedj78/dev-flow","name":"dev-flow","description":"A filesystem contract (.workflow/meta.json) + 50 agent skills that take a product from idea to production: web (Next.js 16) & mobile (Expo/RN), plus an eve agent engine, Linear/scrum, an enforced design-system lint, registry intake and EU data-residency decisions. Runs on Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, Gemini, Cursor.","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":6,"forks":1,"created":"2026-04-25T18:39:02Z","updated":"2026-10-17T18:51:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lukedj78.github.io/dev-flow/","topics":["agent-skills","agentic-workflow","ai-agents","claude-code","code-generation","design-system","eve","expo","gdpr","nextjs","react-native","sdlc","shadcn"],"demo":"https://lukedj78.github.io/dev-flow/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.336Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.336Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.336Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:34:24.914Z","stars":6,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.957Z","stars":6,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-16T13:21:32.384Z","stars":6,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.336Z","stars":6,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React","Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["📖 Browse every skill → — one page per skill: what it does, when it applies, what it deliberately doesn't, and the references it ships. Generated from skills.json, so it can't drift from the suite.","The poster above is the interactive map (dark/light): docs/dev-flow-skill-map.html","The skills are interchangeable consumers of the contract. Tomorrow you could rewrite any of them in TypeScript, swap one out for a Cursor-flavored variant, or extend with your own — as long as they read meta.json and respect the phase semantics, they compose."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lukedj78/dev-flow/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"02f7aed6d9377985c9e750a4e8f586c9d4225fa0d5cc6e74973eaa5df6acc81f","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.438Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.438Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"📖 Browse every skill → — one page per skill: what it does, when it applies, what it deliberately doesn't, and the references it ships. Generated from skills.json, so it can't drift from the suite.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lukedj78/dev-flow/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The agent always stops and asks before allow and approve: it runs the read-only review, shows the report, and waits for a yes to the registry and a yes to the item, whatever the tier and however hurried the prompt. --by names the person who said yes, never the agent or the OS login.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lukedj78/dev-flow/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"With a looser wording, evals/compliance caught the agent allowlisting and approving itself in two sessions out of three, writing the operator's login into --by, so the lock recorded an approval nobody gave.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lukedj78/dev-flow/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"02f7aed6d9377985c9e750a4e8f586c9d4225fa0d5cc6e74973eaa5df6acc81f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lukedj78/dev-flow/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.439Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-17T18:51:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lukedj78/dev-flow/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.445Z","hash":"02f7aed6d9377985c9e750a4e8f586c9d4225fa0d5cc6e74973eaa5df6acc81f","originalBytes":149224,"storedBytes":149224,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:53.336Z","subjects":["Automation & workflows","Mobile","MCP servers & agents","Templates & UI components"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Design","subjects":["Automation & workflow